                <pb facs="1880" n="1706" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v10-12mSupp/pg1706"/>

                <head>667. Memorandum from McNamara to the Chairman of the JCS, April 24, enclosing
                    revision of DOD-State paper entitled “U–2 Flights, Cuba—Contingency
                        Plans”<anchor n="1" xml:id="d667-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <idno type="document-identifier">I–35505/63</idno>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1963-04-24">April 24, 1963</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <pb facs="d667-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d667-1"/>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>DOD-State Paper, “U–2 Flights, Cuba—Contingency Plans”</item>
                </list>
                <p>Attached is a revision of the DOD-State paper incorporating all those changes
                    recommended by JCSM 325–63 which were acceptable to me and the Secretary of
                    State. You will note that subparagraph 3.d. has been reworded in such a way as
                    to meet the concern of the JCS that there be no precommitment against an
                    invasion of Cuba.</p>
                <p>It is anticipated that the paper, in its present form, will be used for
                    discussions with the President at an early date.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed corresp="#p_MRS_1">Robert S. McNamara</signed>
                </closer>
                <pb facs="1881" n="1707" type="typeset" xml:id="pg1707"/>



                <xi:include href="d667-a1.xml" xpointer="d667-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
